@@ -119,9 +119,13 @@ When `snapshot --learn` detects repetitive list or grid items, it groups them in
 
 Learning (`pwa_learn` and the auto-learn in `pwa_snapshot`) keeps user content out of `screens.json`. Live snapshots are not filtered: every element below is still listed with a ref and can be found, clicked or filled.
 
-- **Dynamic content regions.** Elements inside an ARIA `feed`, `log` or `article` never become fields, actions or links. The collector reports the outermost `feed`/`log` ancestor (or an `article`) as the container, and learning folds every element in it into one pattern per item role with `dynamicChildren: true` - even a single element. Address items with the pattern syntax, e.g. `@conversation-with-fede-item(Hello)`.
+- **Dynamic content regions.** Elements inside an ARIA `feed`, `log` or `article`, or inside informal conversation/message lists (`ul`, `ol`, `list`, `grid`, `rowgroup` labeled with conversation/chat/message terms), never become fields, actions or links. The collector reports the outermost dynamic ancestor as the container, and learning folds every element in it into one pattern per item role with `dynamicChildren: true` - even a single element. Address items with the pattern syntax, e.g. `@conversation-with-fede-item(Hello)`.
+- **Anonymous list checkboxes.** `role="checkbox"` elements with an empty or generic selection name inside list, grid, table, rowgroup, feed, log, or article containers are excluded from permanent fields.
 - **Prose.** Outside those regions, an element named from its own text (`nameSource: "content"`) with at least 5 words and ending in `.`, `!`, `?` or `…` is skipped. Labels, `aria-label`, titles and placeholders are never judged as prose.
-- **Transient controls.** Any element whose accent-folded, lowercased name starts with `reaction`, `view reactions`, `quoted message`, `reaccion`, `ver reacciones` or `mensaje citado` is skipped, wherever it sits.
+- **Transient & quick-reaction controls.** Any element whose accent-folded, lowercased name starts with `reaction`, `view reactions`, `quoted message`, `reaccion`, `ver reacciones` or `mensaje citado` is skipped, wherever it sits. Pure emoji controls and quick-reply affirmation chips (e.g. `"¡Felicidades! 🎉"`, `"Me alegro mucho por ti"`, `"Thumbs up"`) are also excluded from permanent screen actions.
+- **User-shared external links & redirectors.** Links pointing to third-party file-sharing or meeting domains (Google Drive, Docs, Meet, Zoom, Teams, Dropbox, Calendly, Loom, Figma, Notion), outbound redirector routes (`/safety/go`), or links whose accessible name is a literal URL are excluded from structural screen links.
+- **Per-message item menus & inline attachments.** Conversation-specific options menus (e.g. `"Abre la lista de opciones en tu conversación con..."`), inline file-attachment download buttons (`"<filename> <size> KB Descargar"`), and repeated per-item `"Más opciones"` / `"More options"` menus (`occurrence >= 1`) are excluded from global screen actions.
+- **Mutable badge & counter suffixes.** Live notification counts and feed reader metrics (e.g. `"Notificaciones, 3 notificaciones nuevas"`, `"Hace 14 horas • 2042 lectores"`) have their volatile numeric suffix scrubbed during semantic `@id` generation (`@notificaciones`) and match resiliently across count changes on re-learn and live resolution.
 
 On re-learn, patterns merge by id: learned patterns replace stored ones with the same id and new ones are added. Entries an older learn persisted (including content the rules above now exclude, and patterns not seen again) are kept, and removed only with `--prune`.
 
